## Useful follow-up prompts

When it is too dark:

```text
Lighten the overall image and lift the workspace shadows, but keep the code editor and WordPress editor UI in dark theme. Preserve the same composition and content.
```

When it is too bright:

```text
Make the image moderately darker and richer, with more premium editorial contrast. Keep it readable and not overly dark. Preserve the same composition and content.
```

When the image feels generic:

```text
Make the planning notes, code, and front-end preview more specific to “[BLOCK NAME].” The image should clearly communicate this exact WordPress / ACF block, not generic web design.
```

When the tones do not match the other hero images:

```text
Adjust the overall tone so it feels like part of the same portfolio hero image series: balanced mid-tone workspace lighting, dark code/editor screens, clean split montage, realistic desk materials, and restrained navy / charcoal accents.
```

When it adds rounded corners:

```text
Remove the rounded outer corners. The image should fill the full 4:3 frame edge-to-edge with square corners.
```

The key phrase to reuse is:

```text
balanced mid-tone lighting, dark code/editor screens, split-panel Plan → Build → Result montage
```
